-- title:
--   A section read as zero on the whole fibre vanishes
-- statement:
--   Let $B_1$ be a commutative local ring with residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,B_1$, and let $V$ be an abelian group carrying a finite $k$-module structure together with a $B_1$-module structure compatible with it via the scalar tower $B_1 \to k$. Let $\iota : V \to B_1$ be $B_1$-linear and injective. Let $f : X \to \operatorname{Spec} B_1$ be a flat morphism of schemes, let $fk : X_k \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and $i : X_k \to X$ be such that the square formed by $i$, $fk$, $f$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue map $B_1 \to k$ is a pullback. Let $U$ be an affine open of $X$, and let $W$ be an open of $X_k$ with $W \le i^{-1}U$ and $i^{-1}U \le W$, i.e. $W = i^{-1}U$. Let $\delta \in \Gamma(X,U)$, and assume `IsFibreReading` holds for the data with the zero map as reading: unfolded, there are $n \in \mathbb{N}$, $v : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to V$ and $s : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \Gamma(X,U)$ with $\sum_j \iota(v_j)\, s_j = \delta$, the products being taken after mapping $\iota(v_j)$ into $\Gamma(X,U)$ along the $B_1$-algebra structure induced by $f$, and such that for every $k$-linear functional $\xi$ on $V$ one has $\sum_j \xi(v_j) \cdot \bigl(i^{\sharp}(s_j)|_W\bigr) = 0$ in $\Gamma(X_k,W)$. The conclusion is $\delta = 0$. The proof uses neither the injectivity of $\iota$ nor the flatness of $f$.
--
--   This is the injectivity half of the bookkeeping for "fibre readings" of sections of an ideal generated by the image of $\iota$: a section of $\Gamma(X,U)$ whose reading over the entire special fibre $i^{-1}U$ vanishes is itself zero. It is used in the small-extension deformation computations for the relative Picard obstruction, namely by [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallExtension.exists_isFibreReading_and_cocycle_one_add_of_forall_d_eq_zero`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmallExtension.exists_isFibreReading_and_cocycle_one_add_of_forall_d_eq_zero), [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallExtension.exists_isInvertible_pullback_iso_of_isPicObstructionCocycle_of_forall_mem_range`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmallExtension.exists_isInvertible_pullback_iso_of_isPicObstructionCocycle_of_forall_mem_range) and [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallExtension.nonempty_iso_unit_of_isPicDeformationCocycle_of_forall_mem_range`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmallExtension.nonempty_iso_unit_of_isPicDeformationCocycle_of_forall_mem_range).
